meta {
  name: Available Orders (auto-search feed)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/orders/available
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Available Orders

  Unclaimed orders reachable from the master's **last known GPS position**,
  matching their categories and inside the order's currently active search
  radius. This is the feed the master app polls (or refreshes on a
  `master.{id}` broadcast) to offer work.

  A master who has never sent a location gets an empty list — a normal state
  right after login, not an error. Send a ping from `06_master_profile` first.

  The client's name and phone are **not** included: the order is not theirs yet.
  They appear after a successful claim.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": [
      {
        "id": 42,
        "category": "Сантехника",
        "city": "Ашхабад",
        "description": "Сломался кран на кухне",
        "address": "Ashgabat, Korogly 12",
        "latitude": 37.95,
        "longitude": 58.38,
        "distance_km": 1.8,
        "search_radius_km": 3,
        "search_started_at": "2026-08-15T10:00:00+05:00",
        "photos": [{ "id": 1, "url": "https://...", "status": "done" }],
        "created_at": "2026-08-15T10:00:00+05:00"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  `search_radius_km` widens over time while the order goes unclaimed, so an
  order out of reach now may show up later.
}
